// P7 L2 boundary for tiles 3 (CRYPTO, PEER 4) and 4 (RoT, PEER 3). M-F1 rev 7 R7.1-R7.3, R7.6, R7.7; SF-1 sec. Design
// (P7); docs/decisions/STEP_C_DESIGN_P7_L2_SHARED.md. Derived from the B-2 trimmed rtl/dual_lane/noc_l2_auth.sv.
//  - Control types 4-7 keep the rev 6 secure wire (R6.5 framing, R6.6 transcript, R6.8 epoch/sequence) and exist only
//    between TILE and PEER; one tx_seq and one rx_seq (the single peer). Data types 0-3 pass through plain (R7.1).
//  - No local KMAC: TX and RX slot P are requesters TX_RID / RX_RID of the shared l2_kmac_engine, which reads their
//    22 transcript words through tx_wd / rx_wd at its index e_widx. Keys live in the engine (T3).
//  - RX (SF-1 P7): slot P takes control packets whose stamped src = PEER (26-flit LUTRAM, HEAD / F0-F4 / MAC words
//    captured to registers while collecting, T1/T4; replay by pointer). Slot G takes every other control packet: a
//    per-source rate limit (one admission per T_RL = 64 cycles, else reason 6), then framing and the header pre-check,
//    then reason 5 (non-peer). G never requests the engine and never replays, so it holds no flit storage at all.
